   "description": "**Question.** After a minute of upward motion, random dots seem to drift downward. How much real downward motion is that illusion worth?\n\n**On screen.** A black cross on white between two round patches of [[param:n_dots]] black dots, [[param:aperture_dva]] across and [[param:aperture_gap_dva]] apart. Adaptation ([[param:initial_adaptation]] at first, then [[param:topup_adaptation]] before every test): left dots all step upward, right dots in random directions. Test, [[param:test_duration]]: in the left patch a share of the dots ([[param:test_levels_pct]] %, + downward, - upward) steps together and the rest randomly; in the right patch [[param:reference_signal_pct]] % step downward.\n\n**The observer.** Keeps looking at the cross (asked, not checked) and then presses the left or right arrow for the patch that looked more coherently downward. No feedback.\n\n**Measured.** The proportion of left choices at each level; a fitted cumulative normal gives the left signal that matches the 40 % reference (PSE). The aftereffect is the control PSE minus this one, in % signal; the paper's was about 40 %.\n\n**Limits.** Display white (15 cd/m2 in the paper) and dot rendering are not calibrated by the software; motion steps are whole frames (1.91 deg/s at 60 Hz). A shifted PSE says nothing about the static aftereffect or where adaptation happens.",
   "sourceFiles": [
    "src/hirisblake1992/task.py",
    "src/hirisblake1992/dvn.py",
    "configs/task.yaml",
    "configs/task-control.yaml",
    "configs/rig-booth.yaml"
   ],
   "notes": [
    "Geometry is the paper's (p. 9025): 3.25-deg displays, nearest edges 4.8 deg apart, cross midway, 100 black 2-arcmin dots on white, ~2 deg/s.",
    "Step 0.0957 deg (the paper's 5 px with an ASSUMED pixel size) every 3 frames at 60 Hz: 1.91 deg/s. The paper's dots cannot have stepped every 67-Hz frame.",
    "ASSUMED: test levels, noise dots take a new random direction each step, signal dots re-drawn each step, wrap along the line of motion at the edge, keys, 5-s answer window after the test, re-adaptation after a 30-s pause.",
    "Not drawn: the aftereffect itself. It is perceived; the arrows mark physical signal directions only."
   ]
  },
