   "description": "**Question.** Without directional adaptation, which left signal looks as coherently downward as the 40 % reference? This is the baseline the adapted PSE is compared with.\n\n**On screen.** As in the adapted set, but during adaptation and every top-up both patches show dots moving in random directions ([[param:adapt_mode]]).\n\n**The observer.** Presses the left or right arrow for the patch that looked more coherently downward.\n\n**Measured.** The PSE, expected near 40 % because the two patches are then physically alike; the paper's unadapted curves were centred there (Fig. 1).\n\n**Limits.** The paper does not describe its no-adaptation display; RDVN in both patches is ASSUMED. Run it as its own session.",
